{"resource":{"id":"rust-practice-questions","title":"Rust — Practice Questions","category":"Programming","difficulty":"Beginner","readingTime":"21 min","pages":39,"lastUpdated":"September 2026","tags":["Programming","Rust","Systems"],"heroImage":"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1461749280684-dccba630e2f6?w=1800&q=80","heroSubtitle":"350+ Rust exercises — MCQs, debugging drills, ownership puzzles, lifetime challenges, output prediction, and mini projects."},"toc":[{"id":"objectives","label":"Learning Objectives"},{"id":"s1","label":"1. MCQs"},{"id":"s2","label":"2. Output Prediction"},{"id":"s3","label":"3. Ownership Puzzles"},{"id":"s4","label":"4. Borrowing Drills"},{"id":"s5","label":"5. Lifetime Challenges"},{"id":"s6","label":"6. Debugging"},{"id":"s7","label":"7. Traits & Generics"},{"id":"s8","label":"8. Concurrency"},{"id":"s9","label":"9. Async Exercises"},{"id":"s10","label":"10. Mini Projects"},{"id":"summary","label":"Summary"},{"id":"faqs","label":"FAQ"},{"id":"glossary","label":"Glossary"},{"id":"references","label":"References"},{"id":"disclaimer","label":"Disclaimer"}],"related":[{"title":"Rust — Answer Key","tag":"Programming","time":"26 min"},{"title":"Rust — Interview Questions","tag":"Programming","time":"35 min"},{"title":"Rust — Complete Tutorial","tag":"Programming","time":"41 min"}],"html":"<section id=\"objectives\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Learning Objectives</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>Practise Rust concept-by-concept with progressive difficulty.</li>\n          <li>Build intuition for the borrow checker through repetition.</li>\n        </ul>\n        <div class=\"my-4 rounded-2xl border-l-4 border-sky-500/40 bg-sky-500/10 text-sky-900 dark:text-sky-100 p-4\"><div class=\"flex items-start gap-3\"><div class=\"mt-0.5 shrink-0\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-5 w-5\"><circle cx=\"12\" cy=\"12\" r=\"10\"/><path d=\"M12 16v-4\"/><path d=\"M12 8h.01\"/></svg></div><div class=\"min-w-0 flex-1\"><p class=\"text-sm font-semibold\">Format</p><div class=\"mt-1 text-sm\">Solutions in the companion \"Rust — Answer Key\" resource.</div></div></div></div>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s1\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">1. MCQs</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={1}>Which is the default variable binding in Rust? (a) mut (b) let (c) const (d) static</Q>\n        <Q n={2}>Rc::clone increments what? (a) new owner (b) reference count (c) memory (d) nothing</Q>\n        <Q n={3}>Which trait allows types to move across threads? (a) Send (b) Sync (c) Copy (d) Drop</Q>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1451187580459-43490279c0fa?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 1 — Progressive-difficulty ladder used across this workbook.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s2\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">2. Output Prediction</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={10}>What prints?<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let s = String::from(&quot;hi&quot;); let t = s; println!(&quot;{}&quot;, t);</code></pre></div></Q>\n        <Q n={11}>What prints?<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let mut v = vec![1,2,3]; v.push(4); println!(&quot;{}&quot;, v.len());</code></pre></div></Q>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s3\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">3. Ownership Puzzles</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={30}>Fix the move-after-use error in this snippet using clone.</Q>\n        <Q n={31}>Return two values from a function without unnecessary allocation.</Q>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s4\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">4. Borrowing Drills</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={60}>Rewrite a function that takes ownership so it borrows instead.</Q>\n        <Q n={61}>Explain why you can't have <code>&amp;T</code> and <code>&amp;mut T</code> live simultaneously.</Q>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s5\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">5. Lifetime Challenges</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={90}>Annotate <code>fn longest(a, b)</code> so it compiles.</Q>\n        <Q n={91}>Explain when you'd use <code>'static</code>.</Q>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s6\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">6. Debugging</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={120}>Find and fix the compile error in this snippet.<div class=\"my-3 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-slate-950 text-slate-100 shadow-sm\"><div class=\"flex items-center justify-between border-b border-white/10 px-4 py-2 text-xs text-slate-400\"><span>python</span></div><pre class=\"overflow-x-auto p-4 text-[13px] leading-relaxed\"><code>let v = vec![1,2,3];\nlet r = &amp;v;\nv.push(4);\nprintln!(&quot;{:?}&quot;, r);</code></pre></div></Q>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s7\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">7. Traits &amp; Generics</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={160}>Implement <code>Display</code> for a <code>Point</code> struct.</Q>\n        <Q n={161}>Write a generic <code>max</code> function bounded by <code>PartialOrd</code>.</Q>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s8\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">8. Concurrency</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={200}>Share a counter across 4 threads using <code>Arc&lt;Mutex&lt;i32&gt;&gt;</code>.</Q>\n        <Q n={201}>Rewrite the same using channels.</Q>\n        <Figure src=\"https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1544197150-b99a580bb7a8?w=1400&q=80\" caption=\"Figure 2 — Concurrency puzzle map: shared state, message passing, and rayon-style data parallelism.\" />\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s9\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">9. Async Exercises</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <Q n={260}>Fetch 10 URLs concurrently with <code>join_all</code>.</Q>\n        <Q n={261}>Add a per-request timeout using <code>tokio::time::timeout</code>.</Q>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"s10\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">10. Mini Projects</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ol class=\"list-decimal space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li>CLI markdown-to-HTML converter.</li>\n          <li>Threaded log tailer.</li>\n          <li>Axum + sqlx Todo API.</li>\n          <li>WebSocket chat server.</li>\n        </ol>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"summary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Summary &amp; Key Takeaways</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p>Practice concept-by-concept; don't jump ahead. Review the Answer Key only after your own attempt.</p>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"faqs\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">FAQ</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <details class=\"group my-2 rounded-2xl border border-border/60 bg-card p-4 open:shadow-sm\"><summary class=\"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 text-sm font-semibold\"><span>Where are the solutions?</span><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"h-4 w-4 shrink-0 transition group-open:rotate-90\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></summary><div class=\"mt-3 text-sm text-muted-foreground\">In the \"Rust — Answer Key\" resource.</div></details>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"glossary\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Glossary</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <ul class=\"list-disc space-y-1 pl-5\">\n          <li><strong>MCQ</strong> — multiple-choice question.</li>\n          <li><strong>Drill</strong> — repeated small exercise for muscle memory.</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"references\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">References</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\"><References /></div></section>\n\n      <section id=\"disclaimer\" class=\"scroll-mt-24 pt-10\"><h2 class=\"text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl\">Disclaimer</h2><div class=\"mt-4 space-y-4 text-foreground/90\">\n        <p class=\"text-sm text-muted-foreground\">Educational workbook. Attempt independently first.</p>\n      </div></section>"}